{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q4642874","formula":"C₃₁H₃₇NO₄","hill":"C31H37NO4","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":31.0,"H":37.0,"N":1.0,"O":4.0},"names":{"en":"7-PET"},"descriptions":{"en":"7-PET is an opioid analgesic drug that has 300 times the potency of morphine by weight. It was discovered by K.W. Bentley and is related to the more well known oripavine derivative etorphine, which is used as a veterinary painkiller and anesthetic medication for the sedation of large animals such as elephants, giraffes, and rhinos. 7-PET itself has a 3-O-methyl ether which reduces potency, but the 3-OH derivative is around 2200 times more potent than morphine, almost the same potency as etorphine as a μ agonist, and unexpectedly the 3-hydrogen compound is also around the same potency of 2000 times morphine."},"fame":5,"pubchemCid":203125,"mass":487.6,"charge":0,"smiles":"C[C@@](CCC1=CC=CC=C1)([C@H]2CC34C=C[C@]2([C@H]5[C@@]36CCN([C@@H]4CC7=C6C(=C(C=C7)OC)O5)C)OC)O","inchikey":"FAIFRACTBXWXGY-WLARPWFJSA-N","iupac":"(2R)-2-[(2S,6R,14R,15S,16R)-11,15-dimethoxy-5-methyl-13-oxa-5-azahexacyclo[13.2.2.12,8.01,6.02,14.012,20]icosa-8(20),9,11,18-tetraen-16-yl]-4-phenylbutan-2-ol","classes":[{"qid":"Q59199015","names":{"en":"group of stereoisomers","ru":"группа стереоизомеров","uk":"група стереоізомерів"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"203125","atoms":73,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":0.339,"y":0.94,"z":1.426,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.683,"y":-1.29,"z":0.961,"el":"O"},{"x":-0.298,"y":1.551,"z":-0.787,"el":"O"},{"x":0.657,"y":3.82,"z":1.165,"el":"O"},{"x":4.35,"y":-2.204,"z":-0.081,"el":"N"},{"x":2.03,"y":-0.682,"z":0.727,"el":"C"},{"x":2.036,"y":-1.5,"z":-0.594,"el":"C"},{"x":0.612,"y":-0.49,"z":1.305,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.379,"y":-1.295,"z":0.408,"el":"C"},{"x":3.526,"y":-1.474,"z":-1.074,"el":"C"},{"x":1.04,"y":-0.894,"z":-1.654,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.405,"y":-0.832,"z":-1.076,"el":"C"},{"x":3.007,"y":